# 102. Artemis Conversational Product UX

The ACCP should support both lightweight access and serious operational work.

## 102.1 Quick Artemis

The compact assistant beside the active page should support tasks such as:

- Quick questions
- Current-page analysis
- Simple inspection
- Simple reversible actions
- Navigation
- Voice input
- Current task status
- Opening a larger workspace

It should remain fast and unobtrusive.

## 102.2 Artemis Workspace / Command Center

A larger expandable or dedicated Artemis workspace should support:

- Full conversation history
- Current context
- Active goals/tasks
- Pending approvals
- Recent actions
- Reports
- Evidence
- Decision details
- Capability/degraded-state visibility
- Operational health
- Financial mandate status
- Admin operations where authorized
- Rollback/recovery actions
- Memory controls where appropriate

The exact information architecture must follow real product needs and verified
capabilities.

## 102.3 Structured Conversational UI

The ACCP should render trusted structured artifacts when text alone would be
unsafe or inefficient.

Examples:

- Approval card
- Task card
- System-health card
- Portfolio status
- Trade/mandate summary
- Before/after diff
- Evidence list
- Capability state
- Failure/recovery state

Do not expose raw internal JSON as the normal user experience.

## 102.4 Action-State Visibility

When Artemis is doing work, the user should be able to distinguish:

- Thinking/analyzing
- Researching
- Waiting
- Awaiting approval
- Executing
- Verifying
- Completed
- Failed
- Rolled back

Do not display a generic loading animation indefinitely.

## 102.5 Accessibility and Localization

The ACCP must follow the normal TitanGold UI standards, including:

- English LTR
- Persian RTL
- Canonical Persian font
- Keyboard use
- Focus management
- Screen-reader semantics
- Responsive layout
- Dark theme
- Mixed-direction technical values
- Accessible approval controls
- Accessible streaming updates

## 102.6 User Control Over Conversation

The user should be able to:

- Stop generation
- Cancel supported tasks
- Clear or archive conversation according to policy
- Inspect pending approvals
- Open relevant canonical product pages
- Disable voice capture
- Understand when Artemis is in degraded mode

